        "original_id": "ace5284f-eee5-5490-b09a-b99cc1679f19",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Aram Saroyan, Edward Keonjian, Strawberry Saroyan, William Saroyan, Carol Matthau\n- Roles: poet, novelist, biographer, memoirist, playwright, engineer\n- Concepts: minimalist poetry, low-power electronics, microelectronics\n- Places: Bolinas, California\n\nFacts:\n- Edward Keonjian was born on 14 August 1909 and died on 6 September 1999.\n- Edward Keonjian was a prominent engineer, an early leader in low-power electronics, and is described as the father of microelectronics.\n- Aram Saroyan was born on September 25, 1943.\n- Aram Saroyan is an American poet, novelist, biographer, memoirist, and playwright.\n- Aram Saroyan is especially known for minimalist poetry, including the one-word poem \"lighght\" and a one-letter poem made from a four-legged version of the letter \"m\".\n- Strawberry Saroyan is the daughter of Aram Saroyan and the granddaughter of playwright William Saroyan and actress Carol Matthau.\n- Strawberry Saroyan spent her childhood in Bolinas, California.",
